1vj2|n|To perceive by the olfactory nerves, or organs of smell; to have a sensation of, excited through the nasal organs when affected by the appropriate materials or qualities; to obtain the scent of; as, to smell a rose; to smell perfumes. ; To detect or perceive, as if by the sense of smell; to scent out; -- often with out. ; To give heed to.	a:1mvg,124,4;lfl,79,6;bw4,64,5;rx8,60,1;1bwg,59,4;200i,55,3;1czq,45,3;1vcj,39,3;lqv,38,1;lfj,38,2;yjq,34,6;1yel,31,6;yok,23,4;1hwq,19,1;bn5,18,5~60f,16,7;lfl,79,6;yjq,34,6;1yel,31,6;bn5,18,5;1gnj,18,5;bw4,64,5;yok,23,4;1mvg,124,4;1bwg,59,4;1czq,45,3;1vcj,39,3;200i,55,3;lfj,38,2;rx8,60,1	v:9qn,48,4;1bwg,39,1;1vcj,23,1~9qn,48,4;1vcj,23,1;1bwg,39,1	V:dzs,36,8;dz1,20,6~dzs,36,8;dz1,20,6	n:1mvg,114,2;14bp,85,3;2mr,78,3;t2q,75,2;28zc,72,5;1zzx,67,4;von,67,4;20vr,64,6;1vkq,58,3;9qn,54,6;lfl,53,1;c3f,53,7;q5,53,6;200i,49,2;1r7d,49,4~c3f,53,7;9qn,54,6;20vr,64,6;q5,53,6;1jda,44,5;28zc,72,5;1zzx,67,4;von,67,4;1r7d,49,4;25jl,35,4;slp,41,4;14bp,85,3;1vkq,58,3;tl5,20,3;ap0,33,3	N:200i,49,2~200i,49,2
